 "description": "A single snapshot of the GEOS model's aerosols on 19 August 2025, played as a sweep from west to east. Each aerosol type is its own instrument: sea salt is a low double bass, dust a clarinet, sulfate an oboe and smoke (black carbon) a harp. An instrument gets louder where its type covers more of the map at that longitude, and higher where it sits further north; a type in both hemispheres plays two notes. Listen for the Saharan dust over the Atlantic and the African smoke plume, loudest near 55 deg W and 17 deg E.",
